1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:06,506
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

2
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:09,801
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

3
00:00:09,884 --> 00:00:12,303
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

4
00:00:12,387 --> 00:00:15,765
♪ One cut, and it’s over ♪

5
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:19,978
[gunshots]

6
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:22,105
Jump, jump, jump,
jump!

7
00:00:22,188 --> 00:00:23,732
Still no word from
Atoy.

8
00:00:23,815 --> 00:00:26,526
Thank you for saving
my life.

9
00:00:26,609 --> 00:00:27,986
Are you Master Cutter?

10
00:00:28,069 --> 00:00:29,070
Atoy!

11
00:00:29,571 --> 00:00:30,572
[grunts]

12
00:00:30,655 --> 00:00:31,865
[thuds, then clatters]

13
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:34,659
[music swells]

14
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:36,703
You've been making things hard for
us for so long.

15
00:00:37,662 --> 00:00:39,205
I'll finish you now!

16
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:39,831
Oh, is that so?

17
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:41,958
I'm the one who’s going to
finish you.

18
00:00:42,041 --> 00:00:43,710
[thumps, then thuds]

19
00:00:43,793 --> 00:00:46,129
[gunshots]

20
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:49,215
Tracker 124, The Master Cutter.

21
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:51,134
Ex Obs, Beatriz Davos.

22
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:52,552
Code name, Belladonna.

23
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:54,971
Beatriz, nice to see
you again.

24
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:57,515
I thought we'd never
see each other again.

25
00:00:58,099 --> 00:00:59,893
Where are Sir Atoy

26
00:00:59,976 --> 00:01:01,061
and Emerson?

27
00:01:01,144 --> 00:01:03,855
Jesabel: They were late for the
family activity.

28
00:01:03,938 --> 00:01:05,231
This is your mommy's favorite.

29
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:05,815
Too late.

30
00:01:06,691 --> 00:01:08,109
Oka already bought one, you know.

31
00:01:08,193 --> 00:01:09,778
Atoy: It looks like you all enjoyed
yourselves.

32
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:11,404
And it doesn't look like
you missed me.

33
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:13,823
Oh, you're the one who has the nerve
to feel hurt?

34
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:15,992
Audrey: At least Oka
is reliable!

35
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:17,577
Even if he's not the father

36
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,788
and husband in this house.

37
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:23,374
Oka is such a showoff, acting
like the hero!

38
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:25,418
Why do they know where
Belladonna is?

39
00:01:26,002 --> 00:01:27,545
[music continues]

40
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:28,379
[phone blipping]

41
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:35,678
I knew it.

42
00:01:36,805 --> 00:01:38,264
Son of a thread.

43
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:40,683
[music swells]

44
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:46,481
[tense music playing]

45
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:52,821
[thuds, then clatters]

46
00:01:54,614 --> 00:01:57,992
I just lost the best man on my team.

47
00:01:59,285 --> 00:02:02,580
And now the two of you are here
telling me nothing.

48
00:02:04,165 --> 00:02:06,584
I am out of patience.

49
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:08,211
So, for your own sake,

50
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:10,755
tell me everything

51
00:02:10,839 --> 00:02:12,715
about the Belladonna.

52
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:15,009
[suspenseful music playing]

53
00:02:15,093 --> 00:02:16,511
Samir: Make them talk!

54
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:18,555
[groans]

55
00:02:26,312 --> 00:02:27,814
[device blipping]

56
00:02:31,484 --> 00:02:31,985
Sir.

57
00:02:32,068 --> 00:02:33,486
[device blipping]

58
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:35,321
The side effects are getting worse.
[electricity buzzing]

59
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:37,490
I don't care. Do it!

60
00:02:37,991 --> 00:02:40,785
Samir: And don't stop until they
recognize me

61
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:42,871
as their boss and
they answer

62
00:02:42,954 --> 00:02:44,998
all of my questions!

63
00:02:45,081 --> 00:02:46,875
[groaning]

64
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:48,543
[electricity buzzing]

65
00:02:48,626 --> 00:02:51,045
Sir, Atoy has found and disconnected
the bug.

66
00:02:51,129 --> 00:02:52,589
[electricity buzzing]

67
00:02:52,672 --> 00:02:53,506
Get out.

68
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,341
Out!

69
00:02:57,719 --> 00:02:59,178
[electricity buzzing]

70
00:02:59,262 --> 00:03:00,430
[music swells]

71
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:01,639
[device blipping]

72
00:03:01,723 --> 00:03:03,600
[electricity buzzing]

73
00:03:03,683 --> 00:03:07,186
[theme music playing]

74
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:10,732
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

75
00:03:10,815 --> 00:03:12,817
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

76
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:18,197
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

77
00:03:18,281 --> 00:03:19,657
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

78
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:21,117
♪ The hole in my polo

79
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:23,661
that's right under the armpit ♪

80
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:25,914
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

81
00:03:25,997 --> 00:03:27,665
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

82
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:29,334
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

83
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:33,838
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

84
00:03:33,922 --> 00:03:34,714
[gunshots]

85
00:03:34,797 --> 00:03:36,674
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

86
00:03:36,758 --> 00:03:39,469
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

87
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:40,386
[music swells]

88
00:03:41,721 --> 00:03:43,765
[music fades]

89
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:47,018
Buddy…

90
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:49,812
[somber music playing]

91
00:03:49,896 --> 00:03:51,814
Buddy, I'm sorry, okay.

92
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:53,107
I hope it's okay with you that I joined

93
00:03:53,191 --> 00:03:54,567
the family day earlier.

94
00:03:56,027 --> 00:03:57,779
The kids really wanted to join
the games, you know.

95
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:00,031
[pensive music playing]

96
00:04:00,114 --> 00:04:01,199
But, buddy, just tell me, if--

97
00:04:01,282 --> 00:04:03,368
if I'm intruding,

98
00:04:03,451 --> 00:04:05,119
if-- if it's too much.

99
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:06,287
No, no. What are you saying?

100
00:04:06,371 --> 00:04:07,372
Buddy, no problem.

101
00:04:07,956 --> 00:04:09,666
I should be the one thanking you.

102
00:04:10,291 --> 00:04:11,918
It's nothing, don't think about it.

103
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:15,546
[music continues]

104
00:04:22,887 --> 00:04:26,224
Karla, have other people been
coming here lately?

105
00:04:26,307 --> 00:04:28,059
Atoy: Has anyone visited lately?

106
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:29,602
It doesn't seem so,
Big Brother.

107
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:31,854
Atoy: Okay.

108
00:04:31,938 --> 00:04:33,314
[music continues]

109
00:04:33,398 --> 00:04:34,315
You see that?

110
00:04:34,399 --> 00:04:36,109
[music continues]

111
00:04:36,192 --> 00:04:37,068
Where did you find this?

112
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:39,028
[music continues]

113
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:40,196
In the car.

114
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:42,240
Do you recognize it?

115
00:04:44,909 --> 00:04:45,868
[music continues]

116
00:04:45,952 --> 00:04:47,120
Transporter?

117
00:04:48,454 --> 00:04:51,124
[music fades]

118
00:04:52,208 --> 00:04:54,877
[suspicious music playing]

119
00:05:03,928 --> 00:05:05,138
Karla: Big Brother Atoy!

120
00:05:05,221 --> 00:05:06,097
Big Brother!

121
00:05:07,974 --> 00:05:11,144
[music continues]

122
00:05:12,145 --> 00:05:13,521
There was a car on standby
there,

123
00:05:13,604 --> 00:05:16,316
and when I went out,
it left.

124
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:19,027
[music continues]

125
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:22,196
Do you think someone is spying
on you, buddy?

126
00:05:23,614 --> 00:05:26,659
[music swells]

127
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:29,329
[music fades]

128
00:05:31,205 --> 00:05:33,291
I really feel like…

129
00:05:35,626 --> 00:05:37,754
he's not telling me something.

130
00:05:38,254 --> 00:05:40,339
Audrey, I think…

131
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:43,634
your husband is telling the truth.

132
00:05:43,718 --> 00:05:46,846
He even has proof, the cake, right?

133
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:50,641
Well, how would I know if it really
came from Batangas?

134
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:53,019
It could have been bought
somewhere nearby.

135
00:05:53,102 --> 00:05:54,812
Oka was able to buy
one, right?

136
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:56,814
Audrey: And the annoying
part is,

137
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:59,400
he's the one who has the nerve
to leave and sulk.

138
00:06:01,319 --> 00:06:02,236
Audrey: Hmm.

139
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:03,905
It's not that…

140
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:06,365
I'm meddling, Audrey,
okay.

141
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:08,910
But I think you were a bit…

142
00:06:08,993 --> 00:06:10,828
over the line earlier.

143
00:06:11,537 --> 00:06:13,623
Atoy was so sad, you know.

144
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:16,501
He already apologized to you,

145
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:18,211
many times even.

146
00:06:18,294 --> 00:06:19,879
[soft drama music playing]

147
00:06:19,962 --> 00:06:22,298
That's the other thing that
irritates me, you know.

148
00:06:23,716 --> 00:06:24,550
He says sorry,

149
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:26,886
but he keeps doing it again
and again.

150
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:32,266
Audrey: He always prioritizes other things
over his own family.

151
00:06:33,601 --> 00:06:36,187
Audrey, there are really a lot of
adjustments,

152
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:40,942
a lot of things will happen where you
won't see eye to eye.

153
00:06:41,025 --> 00:06:47,532
But you'll get through all of that,
as long as you talk things out properly.

154
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:50,159
[sentimental music playing]

155
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:54,205
[object clatters]

156
00:06:54,288 --> 00:06:56,874
Ah, wait a moment.

157
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,376
[pensive music playing]

158
00:06:58,459 --> 00:07:00,169
Make it eight CCTV cameras.

159
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:03,464
Indoor and outdoor.

160
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:05,508
[music continues]

161
00:07:05,591 --> 00:07:08,094
Ah, yes. Include a monitor too.

162
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:10,930
[groans]
[music continues]

163
00:07:11,013 --> 00:07:11,848
[groans]

164
00:07:12,932 --> 00:07:14,434
[groans]
Okay, I'll come by tomorrow.

165
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:17,854
[groans]

166
00:07:33,536 --> 00:07:35,913
[music swells]

167
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:42,920
[door hinge squeaks]

168
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:45,047
[music fades]

169
00:07:51,012 --> 00:07:52,889
Both: I'm sorry.

170
00:07:52,972 --> 00:07:55,057
[soft drama music playing]

171
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:14,035
You should prioritize us.

172
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:15,912
Not your job.

173
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:18,247
[sighs]

174
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:20,041
Sorry, love, okay.

175
00:08:20,666 --> 00:08:22,126
[music continues]

176
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:23,252
I'll make it up to you.

177
00:08:24,295 --> 00:08:25,379
Anyway, I don't want to promise anymore,

178
00:08:25,463 --> 00:08:27,048
I'll just do it.

179
00:08:27,131 --> 00:08:28,716
[music continues]

180
00:08:28,799 --> 00:08:30,718
Thank you so much for all your patience

181
00:08:30,801 --> 00:08:32,094
and understanding, okay.

182
00:08:32,845 --> 00:08:38,100
You know, honestly, sometimes I run
out of patience with you.

183
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:44,524
And then, I get annoyed so quickly.
[music continues]

184
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:46,734
Sorry, love, okay.

185
00:08:46,817 --> 00:08:48,236
[music continues]

186
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:49,654
Miss Cita is right.

187
00:08:50,863 --> 00:08:53,533
We need to communicate everything
properly.

188
00:08:55,618 --> 00:08:56,786
As for me, this is the
only thing I want

189
00:08:56,869 --> 00:08:57,828
to communicate to you.

190
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:03,209
[sentimental music playing]

191
00:09:05,253 --> 00:09:06,337
I love you.

192
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:07,505
[music continues]

193
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:09,131
I love you…

194
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:11,425
you and the kids.

195
00:09:11,509 --> 00:09:13,219
[chuckles softly]

196
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:18,641
[music continues]

197
00:09:21,310 --> 00:09:22,061
[Audrey chuckles softly]

198
00:09:22,144 --> 00:09:25,940
[light music playing]

199
00:09:38,536 --> 00:09:39,745
[smooches]

200
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:40,371
Love…

201
00:09:40,454 --> 00:09:41,664
Yeah?

202
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:42,331
[music fades]

203
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:43,708
I have a surprise for you.

204
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:45,251
Stay right here, okay.

205
00:09:45,334 --> 00:09:46,168
Atoy: Mmm-hmm.

206
00:09:46,752 --> 00:09:47,878
Stay right here.

207
00:09:47,962 --> 00:09:50,923
[pleasant music playing]

208
00:10:03,227 --> 00:10:05,563
Audrey: Love…

209
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:10,026
[music fades]

210
00:10:13,070 --> 00:10:13,779
[Atoy snores]

211
00:10:17,908 --> 00:10:18,451
Love?

212
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,495
[Atoy snores]

213
00:10:21,871 --> 00:10:22,872
Audrey: Love!

214
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:24,874
[snoring]

215
00:10:24,957 --> 00:10:25,875
[light music playing]

216
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:27,126
Love!

217
00:10:27,209 --> 00:10:27,877
[snoring]

218
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:29,503
Wake up, will you.

219
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:31,964
[music continues]

220
00:10:32,048 --> 00:10:33,758
It's just once in
a blue moon!

221
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:36,886
Love, gosh.

222
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:37,637
[clicks tongue]

223
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:39,347
What is this?

224
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:57,948
I saw him wearing
this before.

225
00:10:59,241 --> 00:11:02,828
But maybe there's just
another one like it?

226
00:11:02,912 --> 00:11:04,205
Gotcha!
[table thuds]

227
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:05,331
What do you mean, “gotcha”?!

228
00:11:05,956 --> 00:11:07,875
You startled me!

229
00:11:07,958 --> 00:11:09,335
Sir, look at this.

230
00:11:10,086 --> 00:11:11,337
Look, Sir.

231
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:13,881
Shugo: Atoy went inside the
laundry shop,

232
00:11:13,964 --> 00:11:17,468
but we didn't see him come out.

233
00:11:19,261 --> 00:11:20,846
[sneaky music playing]

234
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:21,722
Wait, this is it.

235
00:11:22,723 --> 00:11:23,933
It's really his.

236
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:25,518
[music fades]

237
00:11:25,601 --> 00:11:28,020
Sir, do you think
he's the one

238
00:11:28,104 --> 00:11:29,647
who burned the laundry shop?

239
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:32,400
[sneaky music playing]

240
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:38,531
The bloodied gown that
Uno was wearing

241
00:11:39,657 --> 00:11:40,699
was found… at the laundry shop.

242
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:42,326
[music continues]

243
00:11:43,035 --> 00:11:45,329
And Atoy was also seen

244
00:11:45,413 --> 00:11:47,957
at Mercado's party,

245
00:11:48,958 --> 00:11:50,084
and then--

246
00:11:50,709 --> 00:11:51,377
Sitcom?

247
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:52,878
[music fades]

248
00:11:52,962 --> 00:11:53,921
And then,

249
00:11:55,005 --> 00:11:57,299
he was also seen where Uno
was hiding.

250
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:58,217
Hmm.

251
00:11:58,884 --> 00:11:59,927
[sneaky music playing]

252
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:06,767
It's likely that he's the one who
burned the laundry shop

253
00:12:07,685 --> 00:12:11,397
to eliminate the
known survivor

254
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,899
of Mercado's party, Uno!

255
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:15,526
[music fades]

256
00:12:15,609 --> 00:12:16,444
Could be.

257
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:20,865
[cackling]

258
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:22,533
Now…

259
00:12:23,617 --> 00:12:26,412
we'll corner you soon, Atoy.

260
00:12:26,495 --> 00:12:28,038
You have no way out.

261
00:12:28,122 --> 00:12:29,498
[cackling]

262
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:34,128
[music continues]

263
00:12:34,211 --> 00:12:35,254
[coughing]

264
00:12:35,337 --> 00:12:36,130
Sir?

265
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:40,259
[coughing]

266
00:12:40,342 --> 00:12:41,427
[music continues]

267
00:12:42,052 --> 00:12:42,887
Mmm. Here, look.

268
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:43,888
Perfect.

269
00:12:43,971 --> 00:12:46,223
Here, let's just divide
this up too.

270
00:12:47,141 --> 00:12:48,893
The avocados are here.

271
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:50,603
Oh, for you.

272
00:12:50,686 --> 00:12:51,687
Thank you!

273
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:52,438
Oh, there!

274
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:56,317
I wonder if Atoy was like this when he
was just starting out?

275
00:12:57,610 --> 00:12:58,402
What matters is

276
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:00,821
we still have blessings.

277
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:02,448
And this avocado is
so delicious!

278
00:13:02,531 --> 00:13:03,407
Emerson: Exactly! Correct

279
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:04,783
You know, Ame…

280
00:13:05,993 --> 00:13:06,869
that's what I like about you.

281
00:13:07,578 --> 00:13:08,746
You're always positive.

282
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:12,124
[playful music playing]

283
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:15,127
What?!

284
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:18,297
Nothing! I'm just observing.

285
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:19,173
Well, well…

286
00:13:19,256 --> 00:13:20,257
[Paldo chuckles]

287
00:13:20,341 --> 00:13:22,009
Siony: Emerson?
Emerson!

288
00:13:22,092 --> 00:13:23,844
Other: Miss Siony!

289
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:25,804
I have a client for you guys!

290
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:27,556
This is my cousin!

291
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:28,641
Oh. Hi, Sis Tess!

292
00:13:28,724 --> 00:13:29,350
It's Sis Tess!

293
00:13:29,433 --> 00:13:31,435
Ah, good day, ah…

294
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:32,770
welcome to our office.

295
00:13:32,853 --> 00:13:34,104
Is there anything we can do for you?

296
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:35,272
Did you lose something?

297
00:13:35,356 --> 00:13:36,941
[wails]

298
00:13:37,816 --> 00:13:39,985
My husband's honesty!

299
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:41,028
[wails]

300
00:13:41,111 --> 00:13:45,115
I want you guys to look for proof of how
he's been cheating on me!

301
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:46,534
[wails]

302
00:13:46,617 --> 00:13:47,451
[sobs]

303
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:49,328
Here, look.

304
00:13:49,411 --> 00:13:50,579
This is Elvis!

305
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:52,206
My-- my scumbag of a husband!

306
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:53,332
[wailing]

307
00:13:54,333 --> 00:13:55,543
And this one,

308
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:56,919
his slutty mistress!

309
00:13:57,002 --> 00:13:57,545
Oh?

310
00:13:57,628 --> 00:13:59,380
Rochelle is the name of that tramp!

311
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:02,591
[wailing]

312
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:07,137
I don't even know why having a mistress
at work is so common these days!

313
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:11,850
Where did the brains of people who
get involved with married men go?!

314
00:14:12,726 --> 00:14:13,519
That's it!

315
00:14:13,602 --> 00:14:15,521
Maybe that's what you should
look for?

316
00:14:15,604 --> 00:14:18,107
The missing brain cells

317
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:20,317
of those skanky fools! That's it!

318
00:14:20,401 --> 00:14:21,694
Oh, oh-- these days,

319
00:14:21,777 --> 00:14:24,446
it's quite hard to find brain
cells, you know.

320
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:26,532
- Ah, but we'll take care of it.
- Oh, let's write that down.

321
00:14:26,615 --> 00:14:27,783
- We'll take care of it, Ma'am Tess.
- Let's write that down.

322
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:29,368
The-- the what? Write down
the brain cells?

323
00:14:29,451 --> 00:14:30,244
Yes, missing brain cells.

324
00:14:30,327 --> 00:14:31,495
Missing brain cells,
apparently.

325
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:32,329
I hope you can help me.

326
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:33,622
Missing brain cells.

327
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:35,124
Okay, okay. Brain cells.

328
00:14:35,207 --> 00:14:37,084
[Emerson chuckles sarcastically]

329
00:14:37,751 --> 00:14:38,252
Missing…

330
00:14:38,335 --> 00:14:39,628
[Emerson sighs]

331
00:14:39,712 --> 00:14:41,338
Don't we have any other--
[overlapping chatter][overlapping chatter]

332
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:42,381
Don't we have any other

333
00:14:42,464 --> 00:14:44,550
more serious cases?

334
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:46,635
Just the real cases, okay.

335
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:48,512
The same level as the cases
of Master Cutter.

336
00:14:48,596 --> 00:14:49,889
[chuckles sarcastically]

337
00:14:49,972 --> 00:14:51,265
This is a blessing, a blessing.

338
00:14:51,348 --> 00:14:53,267
Siony: You can do it; you can do it.

339
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:56,437
[indistinct chattering]

340
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:58,188
[music fades]
[gate hinge squeaks]

341
00:15:03,944 --> 00:15:04,778
Oscar: Buddy!

342
00:15:07,448 --> 00:15:09,074
Are you sure? You'll really be
the one driving?

343
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:11,285
Yes. Ah, I'll take care of it,

344
00:15:11,368 --> 00:15:13,454
so I can really make
it up to Wifey.

345
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:15,331
I'll take care of it,
thank you.

346
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:18,334
Shugo: Hello!
Anybody home!

347
00:15:19,752 --> 00:15:21,503
[sneaky music playing]

348
00:15:21,587 --> 00:15:22,421
Just a moment.

349
00:15:29,136 --> 00:15:30,137
Yes, Sir!

350
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:31,055
Good day.

351
00:15:31,847 --> 00:15:34,308
Good day, Sir Anthony Padua.

352
00:15:35,559 --> 00:15:37,436
We'd like to invite you to
the station again.

353
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:39,188
Oh, well…

354
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:40,856
do you have a warrant now?

355
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:42,900
Because if not,

356
00:15:43,692 --> 00:15:45,235
my answer to you is still the same.

357
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:48,447
I have the right to refuse
your invitation.

358
00:15:48,530 --> 00:15:51,533
Sir, you always refuse, ah.

359
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:53,494
Shugo: Are you hiding
something?

360
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:56,205
We have evidence connecting
you to the case.

361
00:15:56,830 --> 00:15:59,249
So please, sir, just cooperate.

362
00:16:00,167 --> 00:16:02,753
[soft rock music playing]

363
00:16:02,836 --> 00:16:03,337
Buddy.

364
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:04,254
No--

365
00:16:04,838 --> 00:16:06,048
Why don't you just go with them?

366
00:16:07,091 --> 00:16:08,342
If Audrey sees this,

367
00:16:08,425 --> 00:16:09,885
it'll be a bigger mess.

368
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:12,888
[suspicious music playing]

369
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:18,811
Mmm, okay.

370
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:21,063
I'll go with you.

371
00:16:22,064 --> 00:16:23,065
Buddy, I'll leave Audrey
to you.

372
00:16:23,565 --> 00:16:25,818
Just tell her I just went
to the station.

373
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:27,569
Thank you.

374
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:29,446
Let's go.

375
00:16:30,948 --> 00:16:34,410
[music continues]

376
00:16:34,785 --> 00:16:36,412
Are we going to the station or not?

377
00:16:37,037 --> 00:16:40,124
[music swells]

378
00:16:43,085 --> 00:16:44,378
[music fades]

379
00:16:45,462 --> 00:16:47,131
Love, I'm ready!

380
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:51,427
Oh? Where's Atoy?

381
00:16:52,302 --> 00:16:54,179
He's not here, he just had something
to take care of.

382
00:16:54,263 --> 00:16:55,264
Did he say why?

383
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:57,099
He didn't say either.

384
00:16:57,850 --> 00:17:00,227
I thought he'd take me to
where I’m going?

385
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:01,478
Do you want me to take you instead?

386
00:17:01,562 --> 00:17:05,315
[heavy music playing]

387
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:13,073
This, a tailor's tool that was seen at
Mercado's party venue.

388
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:14,783
[sneaky music playing]

389
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:15,617
Wow.

390
00:17:15,701 --> 00:17:18,912
And this one, your necklace.

391
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:20,039
Isn't this yours?

392
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:24,626
This was found at the laundry shop

393
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:25,669
you burned!

394
00:17:26,587 --> 00:17:28,088
Oh, Sir.

395
00:17:28,756 --> 00:17:29,798
[chuckles sarcastically]

396
00:17:29,882 --> 00:17:32,134
I don't know anything about what
you're saying, Sir.

397
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:34,094
Atoy: Wow, that’s so cool.

398
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:36,013
Really? So, what is this?

399
00:17:38,474 --> 00:17:40,768
Shugo: Why were you inside
the laundry shop?

400
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:44,605
Why are you targeting the survivor
of the party?

401
00:17:44,688 --> 00:17:46,356
What are you hiding, huh?

402
00:17:47,608 --> 00:17:49,485
Are you accusing my client?!

403
00:17:50,527 --> 00:17:51,904
Ah, who are you?

404
00:17:51,987 --> 00:17:53,197
Um, my attorney.

405
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:55,949
Attorney, ah, Worcestershire.

406
00:17:57,451 --> 00:17:58,118
Worc--

407
00:17:58,202 --> 00:17:59,745
Worcester-- worcester--

408
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:01,371
Worc-- worcestershire.

409
00:18:01,455 --> 00:18:01,955
The soy sauce?

410
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:02,873
That's correct.

411
00:18:03,373 --> 00:18:04,416
Listen, gentlemen.

412
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:05,918
Let's make one thing clear.

413
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:06,710
[Atoy clears throat]

414
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:09,880
My client has certain inalienable

415
00:18:09,963 --> 00:18:12,508
constitutional rights
that he is able to have.

416
00:18:12,591 --> 00:18:13,717
The right to remain silent,

417
00:18:13,801 --> 00:18:16,261
as well, has the right to
retain competent

418
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:18,347
and independent legal
counsel

419
00:18:18,430 --> 00:18:21,308
during custodial interrogations.

420
00:18:21,391 --> 00:18:23,477
And as here for tremendous
legal counsel,

421
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,562
I am formally advising
my client,

422
00:18:26,063 --> 00:18:28,023
do not answer any further
questions.

423
00:18:29,858 --> 00:18:32,069
Um, we have evidence.

424
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:33,779
Evidence does not suspend

425
00:18:33,862 --> 00:18:36,448
the constitutional rights of the
individual, Officer!

426
00:18:36,532 --> 00:18:37,366
You know that.

427
00:18:38,283 --> 00:18:41,036
Now, this is what I would like to know.

428
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:43,288
Is my client under arrest?

429
00:18:43,372 --> 00:18:45,749
And if so, what are the legal grounds

430
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:51,463
And if not so, what is the current legal
basis for keeping him here now?

431
00:18:51,547 --> 00:18:53,674
[playful music playing]

432
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:54,842
Sir…

433
00:18:56,051 --> 00:18:56,844
nosebleed.

434
00:18:56,927 --> 00:18:57,594
[music continues]

435
00:19:04,309 --> 00:19:05,269
[gasps]

436
00:19:05,352 --> 00:19:06,395
This isn't a nosebleed.

437
00:19:07,104 --> 00:19:08,397
I'm already stressed.

438
00:19:09,439 --> 00:19:11,817
[music swells]

439
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:18,532
Post this around the venue, okay.

440
00:19:18,615 --> 00:19:21,535
Boys, Aira, post it at the
entrance. Okay?

441
00:19:21,618 --> 00:19:23,996
Thank you.
That's it, Francine.

442
00:19:24,496 --> 00:19:26,832
Yes, Ms. Audrey!

443
00:19:26,915 --> 00:19:29,168
It's also posted and
the digital copy

444
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:31,211
is also up for sharing on
our social media page!

445
00:19:31,295 --> 00:19:32,254
- Great job!
- Yes.

446
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:33,630
Of course! I got this.

447
00:19:33,714 --> 00:19:35,007
Siony: Jona!

448
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:35,883
- Hey.
- Siony: Jona!

449
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:37,134
Here's your lunch order!

450
00:19:37,217 --> 00:19:38,635
Both: Miss Siony!

451
00:19:38,719 --> 00:19:40,554
- Hello!
- Hi, Audrey!

452
00:19:40,637 --> 00:19:42,097
Oka referred me here.

453
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:44,641
I'm accredited to sell food
here now.

454
00:19:44,725 --> 00:19:45,934
Oka is really the best!

455
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:47,144
So fancy!

456
00:19:47,227 --> 00:19:51,648
Hey, tell your co-workers to order
from me, so you don't have to go out.

457
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:52,733
Oh, I'll take care of that.

458
00:19:52,816 --> 00:19:53,817
Give me this, hmm.

459
00:19:53,901 --> 00:19:55,194
Jona: Over here.

460
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:56,111
Siony: Thank you.

461
00:19:58,906 --> 00:20:00,824
Oh, my god!

462
00:20:00,908 --> 00:20:01,742
[clicks tongue]

463
00:20:01,825 --> 00:20:04,786
Siony: My cousin is so stubborn!

464
00:20:05,579 --> 00:20:07,164
That's why I'm telling
you, Audrey,

465
00:20:07,247 --> 00:20:09,208
keep an eye on Atoy!

466
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:11,168
Keep an eye?

467
00:20:11,251 --> 00:20:12,336
Siony: Mmm-hmm.

468
00:20:12,419 --> 00:20:13,295
[titters]

469
00:20:13,378 --> 00:20:14,171
Well, why?

470
00:20:14,671 --> 00:20:19,635
Because my cousin is going crazy because
her husband has a mistress!

471
00:20:19,718 --> 00:20:20,802
[Oscar scoffs]

472
00:20:22,512 --> 00:20:23,972
Ah, really?

473
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:24,973
Siony: Mmm-hmm.

474
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:26,767
How did she find out?

475
00:20:27,559 --> 00:20:28,977
Through text.

476
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:31,313
But she said there were already
many red flags.

477
00:20:31,396 --> 00:20:33,607
Siony: Oh, he says
he’s busy.

478
00:20:33,690 --> 00:20:36,026
But she doesn't know
where he goes,

479
00:20:36,109 --> 00:20:39,821
he's always talking to someone else
and texting someone else.

480
00:20:39,905 --> 00:20:43,242
And he brings his phone
even to the bathroom.

481
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:44,368
And also…

482
00:20:46,119 --> 00:20:47,412
she said they're no longer…

483
00:20:48,121 --> 00:20:49,748
doing the loving-loving.

484
00:20:49,831 --> 00:20:51,959
[tense music playing]

485
00:20:52,542 --> 00:20:53,543
Audrey: Love!

486
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:54,711
[snoring]

487
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:56,880
[music continues]

488
00:20:57,464 --> 00:21:00,050
[snoring]

489
00:21:00,133 --> 00:21:02,052
What is this? Love!

490
00:21:02,886 --> 00:21:04,263
Wake up, will you.

491
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:06,974
[music continues]

492
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:08,600
It's only once in a blue moon!

493
00:21:10,435 --> 00:21:13,146
[music swells]

494
00:21:15,482 --> 00:21:18,860
And then the man still won't admit it!

495
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:20,862
He even tries to get away with it!

496
00:21:20,946 --> 00:21:23,907
Siony: That's why you really need
strong evidence

497
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:26,243
or to catch him
in the act!

498
00:21:26,326 --> 00:21:27,536
[pensive music playing]

499
00:21:27,619 --> 00:21:29,705
So, wait, Miss Siony, this…

500
00:21:30,706 --> 00:21:32,666
mistress of your cousin's
husband…

501
00:21:33,417 --> 00:21:35,127
… does your cousin know her?

502
00:21:35,210 --> 00:21:39,298
Yes! His coworker!

503
00:21:39,381 --> 00:21:40,590
Siony: And there's more, okay.

504
00:21:40,674 --> 00:21:44,970
The woman even wanted to befriend
her before,

505
00:21:45,512 --> 00:21:49,516
because she wanted to know
the wife's moves!

506
00:21:49,599 --> 00:21:50,475
Siony: Oh, right?

507
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:51,685
So, Audrey, oh my.

508
00:21:51,768 --> 00:21:54,229
Good thing there are many
guards at the shop.

509
00:21:54,313 --> 00:21:56,398
Miss Siony, you’re such
a blabbermouth.

510
00:21:56,481 --> 00:21:57,941
Atoy isn't like that!

511
00:21:58,025 --> 00:21:59,109
He's loyal to Audrey,

512
00:21:59,192 --> 00:22:00,193
you can even ask his
best friend.

513
00:22:00,277 --> 00:22:01,611
Right, Baby Oka?

514
00:22:01,987 --> 00:22:03,113
Yes, Baby Jona.

515
00:22:03,739 --> 00:22:04,698
Don't be jealous, okay.

516
00:22:04,781 --> 00:22:06,074
Oscar: Of course.

517
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:06,700
You know, Audrey,

518
00:22:07,242 --> 00:22:08,869
Atoy would never do
that to you.

519
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:12,331
Because he knows
you're the…

520
00:22:12,414 --> 00:22:15,792
kind of woman who
should be valued…

521
00:22:17,252 --> 00:22:19,046
truly loved.

522
00:22:19,129 --> 00:22:20,589
[pensive music playing]

523
00:22:20,672 --> 00:22:23,342
Baby Oka, do you value me?

524
00:22:24,509 --> 00:22:25,343
Of course.

525
00:22:25,927 --> 00:22:26,970
Don't be jealous.

526
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:28,138
You, have some rice.

527
00:22:28,221 --> 00:22:30,015
Me, do you appreciate
me, Oka?

528
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:32,184
Of course, as long as I
to get pak--

529
00:22:32,267 --> 00:22:33,393
I'll have pinakbet later.

530
00:22:33,477 --> 00:22:34,936
Oh, your pakbet is free.

531
00:22:35,353 --> 00:22:36,188
Yes!

532
00:22:36,271 --> 00:22:37,481
[music fades]

533
00:22:38,482 --> 00:22:39,649
[door closes]

534
00:22:40,692 --> 00:22:43,612
- Chief, Chief! Yes.
- Oh, Attorney.

535
00:22:43,695 --> 00:22:45,238
I would advise you that in the future,

536
00:22:45,947 --> 00:22:47,574
you tell your guards and officers

537
00:22:47,657 --> 00:22:49,951
that if they're to conduct custodial
interrogations

538
00:22:50,035 --> 00:22:51,495
that they should
be carried out

539
00:22:51,578 --> 00:22:55,457
in full accordance with the constitutional
rights of the suspect.

540
00:22:56,124 --> 00:22:58,543
Furthermore, I think you should
have a word

541
00:22:58,627 --> 00:23:01,588
with Mr. Matangbaka and his colleague,
Shugo, because…

542
00:23:02,130 --> 00:23:03,256
I would hate for this to have--

543
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:04,257
to turn into…

544
00:23:05,050 --> 00:23:06,718
an administrative complaint.

545
00:23:06,802 --> 00:23:07,803
Okay, Attorney.

546
00:23:07,886 --> 00:23:08,637
I'll talk to them.

547
00:23:09,096 --> 00:23:09,971
Thank you, Chief.

548
00:23:10,847 --> 00:23:11,890
[soft rock music playing]

549
00:23:11,973 --> 00:23:13,141
[door lock clicks]

550
00:23:13,225 --> 00:23:15,310
[music continues]

551
00:23:15,393 --> 00:23:15,894
[door closes]

552
00:23:15,977 --> 00:23:17,687
Wow. You were great there, ah.

553
00:23:17,771 --> 00:23:18,605
[sighs]

554
00:23:19,272 --> 00:23:22,943
[rock music playing]

555
00:23:23,860 --> 00:23:24,861
[car door lock clicks]

556
00:23:27,906 --> 00:23:29,908
[music continues]

557
00:23:29,991 --> 00:23:31,868
Atoy: Brother Kurt, I need your help.

558
00:23:32,661 --> 00:23:34,246
Disguise yourself as my lawyer,

559
00:23:34,746 --> 00:23:36,373
and memorize this script, okay.

560
00:23:37,207 --> 00:23:40,210
My client has the constitutional
right to remain silent…

561
00:23:40,293 --> 00:23:41,253
[music swells]

562
00:23:41,336 --> 00:23:42,838
Where did the other things
you said come from?

563
00:23:42,921 --> 00:23:43,922
Oh, of course,
Brother Atoy,

564
00:23:44,005 --> 00:23:46,341
I asked an online
friend for help.

565
00:23:46,424 --> 00:23:48,051
Because I memorized
a lot, okay.

566
00:23:48,718 --> 00:23:49,636
[gasps]

567
00:23:49,719 --> 00:23:52,055
Great. I'm impressed with you.

568
00:23:52,597 --> 00:23:54,808
What exactly happened
in your interrogation?!

569
00:23:54,891 --> 00:23:57,727
Chief: Why is that lawyer talking
about an admin complaint?!

570
00:23:57,811 --> 00:24:01,064
[playful music playing]

571
00:24:04,317 --> 00:24:05,193
[door closes]

572
00:24:05,277 --> 00:24:07,779
[music fades]

573
00:24:07,863 --> 00:24:09,781
You were the last one
Mercado protected

574
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:10,907
before he disappeared.

575
00:24:13,618 --> 00:24:15,453
What do you know about Obsidian?

576
00:24:16,037 --> 00:24:18,832
I only know little details but not
the big picture.

577
00:24:20,041 --> 00:24:22,669
I make custom-made weapons.

578
00:24:22,752 --> 00:24:24,212
One of my last tasks for Obsidian

579
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:26,798
was to create specialized
long-ranged guns.

580
00:24:26,882 --> 00:24:28,466
Part of the Big Bang
Plot apparently.

581
00:24:28,967 --> 00:24:31,678
[suspicious music playing]

582
00:24:33,471 --> 00:24:34,848
What could that Big Bang be?

583
00:24:35,932 --> 00:24:37,267
Honestly, beats me.

584
00:24:37,809 --> 00:24:40,270
But before Samir came here
to Manila,

585
00:24:40,353 --> 00:24:42,397
I met with a certain
Sir Ronan.

586
00:24:42,939 --> 00:24:44,691
Belladonna: They call him
The Manager.

587
00:24:44,774 --> 00:24:46,902
He handed over funds for me

588
00:24:46,985 --> 00:24:48,236
in my last task,

589
00:24:49,070 --> 00:24:50,947
and he works for Bank of
the Philippines,

590
00:24:51,031 --> 00:24:52,115
Balingbing Branch.

591
00:24:54,409 --> 00:24:56,369
So-- so, he's a bank manager?

592
00:24:57,329 --> 00:24:58,580
I wouldn't say that.

593
00:24:58,663 --> 00:25:00,916
Not your ordinary
bank manager.

594
00:25:01,833 --> 00:25:03,251
He's the one who
facilitates

595
00:25:03,335 --> 00:25:08,131
the release of large funds without anyone
at the bank noticing.

596
00:25:09,090 --> 00:25:11,259
They release money once or
twice a month,

597
00:25:11,343 --> 00:25:13,762
for Obsidian's operations.

598
00:25:13,845 --> 00:25:15,263
[music fades]

599
00:25:15,347 --> 00:25:17,766
So, he's the one who releases
money from the bank.

600
00:25:18,725 --> 00:25:19,601
Oh, let's follow that,

601
00:25:19,684 --> 00:25:21,394
it could possibly lead us to
the Big Bang.

602
00:25:21,478 --> 00:25:23,355
Can you give me more information
on this Ronan?

603
00:25:24,856 --> 00:25:27,692
Belladonna: Physically, late 30s
to early 40s.

604
00:25:27,776 --> 00:25:28,276
Atoy: Mmm.

605
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:29,277
He likes jewelry,

606
00:25:30,070 --> 00:25:31,112
Belladonna: because he gives it

607
00:25:31,196 --> 00:25:32,155
to his girls.

608
00:25:32,864 --> 00:25:35,408
He has a wife, but he has girls
on the side.

609
00:25:36,034 --> 00:25:37,494
And one thing about him,

610
00:25:37,577 --> 00:25:39,454
is he never lets go of
his phone.

611
00:25:39,537 --> 00:25:41,122
He never lets it out of
his sight.

612
00:25:42,540 --> 00:25:43,250
Atoy: Do you know
what model

613
00:25:43,333 --> 00:25:44,167
his phone is?

614
00:25:44,709 --> 00:25:47,003
[music swells]

615
00:25:47,087 --> 00:25:48,713
Sir, the loan applicant

616
00:25:48,797 --> 00:25:49,965
is here for the interview.

617
00:25:50,048 --> 00:25:50,924
Let him in.

618
00:25:51,549 --> 00:25:54,511
[rock music playing]

619
00:25:54,594 --> 00:25:56,721
Are you Ronan Santos?

620
00:25:57,514 --> 00:26:00,558
[music swells]

621
00:26:00,642 --> 00:26:03,937
[electronic blipping]

622
00:26:04,813 --> 00:26:08,900
[intense music playing]

623
00:26:10,777 --> 00:26:11,403
It's like…

624
00:26:11,486 --> 00:26:12,654
something's wrong, you know.

625
00:26:13,238 --> 00:26:16,283
Every time Atoy says he's
at the shop,

626
00:26:16,366 --> 00:26:18,451
Audrey: I'm not sure if he's telling the
truth or not.

627
00:26:18,535 --> 00:26:20,704
It's easy to find out if…

628
00:26:20,787 --> 00:26:22,455
he's really at the
shop or not.

629
00:26:22,539 --> 00:26:25,625
I called you, Tabang Lupa
community,

630
00:26:25,709 --> 00:26:27,585
for this.

631
00:26:27,669 --> 00:26:28,753
So, sign up.

632
00:26:28,837 --> 00:26:30,213
Oh, zombie, zombie!

633
00:26:30,297 --> 00:26:31,339
Samir: What is happening
here?

634
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:32,882
Obsidian lab head: This is a new
side effect.

635
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:34,134
[theme music playing]

636
00:26:34,217 --> 00:26:35,218
Belladonna: Who is F. Cohen?

637
00:26:35,302 --> 00:26:37,554
Frank Cohen, that's
Samir's alias.

638
00:26:37,637 --> 00:26:39,222
'Cause if we can trail that,

639
00:26:39,306 --> 00:26:41,599
maybe they'll lead us to
the Obsidian HQ.

640
00:26:42,142 --> 00:26:45,729
["Mamang Sastre" playing]
